      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We describe the anatomic findings in a 2-year-old patient with double outlet right ventricle with right-sided aorta in the setting of usual atrial arrangement and discordant atrioventricular connections, making comparison with a specimen from the pathological archive of the Birmingham Children's Hospital in the United Kingdom having this rare combination of anatomic features. We discuss the challenges involved in diagnosis and management."},
